      },
      {
        "Id": "c6a74c7802fd49f5ad8b0507109bb538",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  open the SHEET with the elevations / sections on it (or one elevation / section), set RUN = False and run = preview (counts, nothing kept), then RUN = True.   Every elevation / section gets the SD view template (material colour + hatch, grey poche, elements behind fade to grey), a crop around the building, level heads both ends, grid bubbles on top, level chain + overall height, grid chain + overall width, spot levels on roof / parapet tops, door / window tags and material notes on the faces you can see.  Then ONE scale for the sheet (largest that fits) and the viewports packed inside the title block.   VIEWS = ALL does every elevation + section of the project.   Run again = D15's own dims / spots / notes replaced.  Ctrl+Z undoes a run.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
